{"name":"Freezing Vapour","hex":"#d4e9f5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"freezing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Suffering or causing frost.","Very cold."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The change in state of a substance from liquid to solid by cooling to a critically low temperature.","The action of numbing with anesthetics."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/freezing"},{"term":"vapour","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["British standard spelling of vapor."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["British standard spelling of vapor."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vapour"}],"entries":[{"title":"Freezing","blocks":[{"text":"Freezing is a phase transition in which a liquid turns into a solid when its temperature is lowered below its freezing point."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0c/Light_glinting_off_icicles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Freezing"},{"title":"Vapor","blocks":[{"text":"In physics, a vapor or vapour is a substance in the gas phase at a temperature lower than its critical temperature, which means that the vapor can be condensed to a liquid by increasing the pressure on it without reducing the temperature of the vapor. A vapor is different from an aerosol. An aerosol is a suspension of tiny particles of liquid, solid, or both within a gas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Nitrogen_dioxide_gas.jpg/330px-Nitrogen_dioxide_gas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vapor"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Vapor_being_used_in_a_cloud_chamber.jpg/500px-Vapor_being_used_in_a_cloud_chamber.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Vapor_being_used_in_a_cloud_chamber.jpg/1280px-Vapor_being_used_in_a_cloud_chamber.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Vapor_being_used_in_a_cloud_chamber.jpg/500px-Vapor_being_used_in_a_cloud_chamber.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"If the vapor pressure exceeds the equilibrium value, it becomes supersaturated and condenses on any available nucleation sites e. g. particles of dust. This principle is used in cloud chambers, where particles of radiation are visualized because they nucleate formation of water droplets.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVapor_being_used_in_a_cloud_chamber.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Crepuscular_Rays_Beam_through_the_Mist_Blown_from_Takkakaw_Falls.jpg/500px-Crepuscular_Rays_Beam_through_the_Mist_Blown_from_Takkakaw_Falls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Crepuscular_Rays_Beam_through_the_Mist_Blown_from_Takkakaw_Falls.jpg/1280px-Crepuscular_Rays_Beam_through_the_Mist_Blown_from_Takkakaw_Falls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Crepuscular_Rays_Beam_through_the_Mist_Blown_from_Takkakaw_Falls.jpg/500px-Crepuscular_Rays_Beam_through_the_Mist_Blown_from_Takkakaw_Falls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Invisible water vapor condenses to form visible water droplets called mist","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACrepuscular_Rays_Beam_through_the_Mist_Blown_from_Takkakaw_Falls.jpg"}],"sounds":{"freezing":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4e/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Persent101-freezing.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_camp